WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.150
This is Allen Company training on the Federal Mine

00:07.150 --> 00:10.862
Safety and Health Act of 1977, the law that created

00:10.862 --> 00:14.300
MSHA and the rights you have as a miner.

00:14.300 --> 00:17.312
Part 48 requires that we discuss Section 2 of the

00:17.312 --> 00:20.463
Act, and how supervisors and miners' representatives

00:20.463 --> 00:22.637
fit into safety at the mine.

00:23.748 --> 00:26.498
Section 2 is Congress's statement of why the law

00:26.498 --> 00:29.773
exists. It says the first priority and concern

00:29.773 --> 00:32.810
of everyone in mining must be the health and safety

00:32.810 --> 00:35.761
of its most precious resource: the miner.

00:35.761 --> 00:38.310
It finds that deaths and serious injuries from

00:38.310 --> 00:41.461
unsafe conditions cause grief and suffering and

00:41.461 --> 00:43.723
are a serious drain on the economy.

00:43.723 --> 00:46.560
It says operators, with the help of miners,

00:46.560 --> 00:49.610
have the primary responsibility to prevent unsafe

00:49.610 --> 00:52.185
and unhealthy conditions. And it says there's a

00:52.185 --> 00:55.898
need for mandatory standards, enforced by the government,

00:55.898 --> 00:57.398
to protect miners.

00:58.518 --> 01:01.456
In plain terms: Allen is responsible for providing

01:01.456 --> 01:04.505
a safe mine, and you're part of making it safe.

01:04.505 --> 01:07.393
That means following the rules, reporting hazards,

01:07.393 --> 01:09.543
and stopping work that isn't safe.

01:10.656 --> 01:13.206
At your site, the line of authority runs from the

01:13.206 --> 01:15.806
superintendent and site manager, through the mine

01:15.806 --> 01:18.493
foreman and your supervisor, to you.

01:18.493 --> 01:21.006
Your supervisor is responsible for examining your

01:21.006 --> 01:24.043
work area, assigning tasks you're trained for,

01:24.043 --> 01:27.093
and correcting hazards. The Safety Manager supports

01:27.093 --> 01:28.156
every site.

01:29.274 --> 01:31.999
Miners can choose a representative of miners.

01:31.999 --> 01:34.699
Two or more miners can designate one,

01:34.699 --> 01:37.411
and it's filed with MSHA under Part 40.

01:37.411 --> 01:40.286
The representative can accompany MSHA inspectors

01:40.286 --> 01:43.061
on inspections, can request inspections,

01:43.061 --> 01:46.211
and receives copies of certain records and notices.

01:46.211 --> 01:48.549
The representative's role is to speak for miners

01:48.549 --> 01:51.761
on safety and health. Right now, no Allen site

01:51.761 --> 01:54.199
has a designated miners' representative,

01:54.199 --> 01:56.599
but you have the right to designate one.

01:57.744 --> 02:00.282
You have the right to report hazards to Allen or

02:00.282 --> 02:04.282
to MSHA, to request an MSHA inspection if you believe

02:04.282 --> 02:06.719
there's a violation or imminent danger,

02:06.719 --> 02:09.207
to receive the training required by law,

02:09.207 --> 02:12.257
and to be protected from discrimination or retaliation

02:12.257 --> 02:14.869
for exercising these rights. If you think you've

02:14.869 --> 02:17.457
been retaliated against, you can file a complaint

02:17.457 --> 02:19.882
with MSHA within 60 days.

02:21.006 --> 02:23.806
At Allen: if you see a hazard, warn the people

02:23.806 --> 02:26.531
around you, tell your supervisor, and make sure

02:26.531 --> 02:29.231
it's recorded. If it isn't fixed, take it to the

02:29.231 --> 02:30.506
Safety Manager.

02:31.644 --> 02:34.682
The miner comes first. Allen is responsible,

02:34.682 --> 02:37.207
and you help. Know your chain of command and your

02:37.207 --> 02:40.157
representative. You can report, request,

02:40.157 --> 02:41.357
and be protected.

02:42.474 --> 02:45.636
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

02:45.636 --> 02:47.137
override this video.
